  "id": "Compound::DB00431 - Gene::2741",
  "verbalization": "Lindane is implicated in the interaction with Glra3, which is involved in the regulation of ion channels through extracellular glycine or chloride activities. The evidence suggests that Lindane binds to Glra3, which then participates in various ion channel activities, ultimately leading to its participation in the activity of Glra1. This indicates a potential mechanism where Lindane influences the function of Glra1 through its interaction with Glra3, which in turn modulates ion channel activity. The overlapping roles of Glra3 in different ion channel activities highlight the complexity of its involvement in cellular processes, suggesting that Lindane may exert its effects through multiple pathways involving Glra3. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Glra3 in mediating the effects of Lindane on ion channel function, positioning it as a critical intermediary in the relationship between Lindane and Glra1.",
